  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Vulnerable Refugees and Local Communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, Bangladesh, through Improved Access to Health, Protection, Shelter, Site Management and Site Development, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) Services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For the Rohingya in Bangladesh, 2023 marks the sixth year since their mass displacement from Myanmar. While the Government of Bangladesh (GoB) and the international community have maintained the provision of immediate lifesaving assistance, the needs are immense and complex challenges continue to emerge in the response. Almost entirely dependent on humanitarian aid, the possibility of concrete and lasting solutions for the Rohingya refugees remains uncertain. Since the influx of Rohingya people from Myanmar into Bangladesh in August 2017, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) has significantly scaled up its presence and operational response. Through this project, IOM continues to engage in a multi-sectoral response to support vulnerable refugees and local communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar through improved access to Health, Protection, Shelter, Site Management and Site Development, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene services.</narrative>
  </description>
